@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# External SF2 renderer routing
+
+Manually choosing an external `.sf2` now loads that bank into **FluidSynth + RtAudio**. The renderer is no longer inferred from the current output-routing dropdown, so a previously selected `lggm` route cannot silently redirect an external bank into the internal LS-GM sampler. Manual SF2 selection sets the output route to `fluid`; an explicitly selected `both` route remains `both`.
+
+The native renderer remains available for its intended, dedicated paths:
+
+- Yamaha Style-family playback continues to activate the native LS-GM SF2 sampler.
+- Selecting the explicit `LG-GM Native C++ (LS-GM.sf2)` output route still loads LS-GM through the native sampler.
+- Roland `.STL` playback continues to use Native SCVA.
+- Changing RtAudio device/sample-rate/buffer settings preserves the explicitly selected LG-GM route.
+
+A Yamaha Style-family or Roland `.STL` renderer is exclusive while that style is active. The SF2 chooser therefore asks the user to unload that style before replacing its dedicated renderer.
+
+Regression guard: `tests/external_sf2_fluidsynth_routing_source_test.py`.
